{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Please take up.</b> A term of sharpening, as that which we learned: one may not sharpen the knife, but one may pass it over its fellow (Beitzah 28) — sharpen your knife and slaughter well, so that you do not feed me a carcass (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Your weapons.</b> Your sword, which is the way to suspend it." "<b>And hunt for me.</b> From ownerless game, and not from robbery."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:43.025902309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}